Under federal law, children of a member of a statutory health insurance fund are covered through the Familienversicherung (free family cover for dependants) (SGB V §10). This is a general rule; whether your baby is covered is decided by the health insurance fund, not here.

The law covers a member's children if all of the following apply. The child:
1. lives or usually stays in Germany ("Wohnsitz oder gewöhnlichen Aufenthalt im Inland");
2. is not compulsorily insured under the listed provisions of §5 and is not voluntarily insured;
3. is not exempt from insurance or released from compulsory insurance;
4. is not self-employed as a main occupation;
5. has no total income regularly above one seventh of the monthly reference figure ("ein Siebtel der monatlichen Bezugsgröße").

Children are covered up to age 18 ("bis zur Vollendung des achtzehnten Lebensjahres"), with longer periods in the cases the statute lists.

There is one exclusion to know about. Children are not covered this way if the parent related to them who is married to or the civil partner of the member is not a member of a health insurance fund, and that parent's total income regularly exceeds one twelfth of the annual earnings ceiling ("ein Zwölftel der Jahresarbeitsentgeltgrenze") and is regularly higher than the member's income (§10(3)).

If both parents are members and the conditions are met more than once, the member chooses the fund (§10(5)).

What you do: the member must report the covered child to the competent health insurance fund, with the details needed to run the Familienversicherung, and must also report later changes to those details (§10(6)).

You will need the birth certificate. The Familienportal lists registration with the health insurance fund ("Anmeldung bei der Krankenkasse") among the things the birth certificate is needed for. It is issued by the registry office for the place of birth, where the Familienportal says you must register the child within 1 week ("innerhalb 1 Woche"). If the child is born in a hospital, birth centre or maternity clinic, the facility notifies the registry office.

The excerpts do not cover how a child is insured if the Familienversicherung does not apply, for example through private insurance. Ask your health insurance fund about that.
